                        <description>&lt;jats:title&gt;ABSTRACT&lt;/jats:title&gt;                 &lt;jats:p&gt;                   Forest characteristics vary largely at the regional level and in smaller geographic areas in Finland. The amount of greenhouse gas emissions is related to changes in biomass and the soil type (e.g. upland soils vs. peatlands). Spatially accurate map data of forests and biomass changes could improve the ability to suggest optimal management alternatives for any patch of land, e.g. in terms of climate change mitigation. I</description> 
